WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.159
Rectangular fin heat transfer
A worked example connects fin geometry, efficiency, and heat-transfer enhancement.

2
00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:12.198
Count the exposed area
Subtract the fin footprints from the wall and add the exposed fin surfaces.

3
00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:18.228
Apply fin efficiency
The temperature falls along the fin, so its full area does not remain at the base temperature.

4
00:00:18.328 --> 00:00:24.242
Combine fins and exposed wall
The calculation weights fin area by its efficiency before adding the exposed wall contribution.

5
00:00:24.342 --> 00:00:30.277
Use the stated convection coefficients
The bare-wall and finned-wall coefficients differ; area alone does not determine the result.

6
00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:36.149
Check the result and assumptions
The stated finite-fin model gives a 1317.6 percent increase. The walkthrough documents the printed-
answer discrepancy.
